From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:04:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 209/210] codecs: Add MPEG-4 Part 2 and H.263 stateless decoder
 base class

Add GstMpeg4Decoder, a base class for stateless MPEG-4 Part 2
(ISO/IEC 14496-2), H.263 and Sorenson Spark decoders, with
GstMpeg4Picture. The bitstream format follows the sink caps.

It takes one picture per buffer: a VOP with the configuration headers
before it, as mpeg4videoparse outputs them, an H.263 picture from
h263parse, or a Sorenson Spark picture from flvdemux. It gives the
subclass the picture from its start code to its end, the size of its
header, and its forward and backward references.

For MPEG-4 it parses the video object layers (also from codec_data),
the group of VOP time codes and the encoder identification in the user
data, from which it derives the encoder deviations a decoder has to
reproduce, as libavcodec does. It keeps the VOP times to give B-VOPs
their TRB and TRD, frame and field based, skips not coded VOPs and
B-VOPs whose times do not fit their references, and finds the size of
vop_time_increment from the VOP when the layer gets it wrong. VOPs are
output in display order: B-VOPs at once, other VOPs when the next one
of them is decoded, or at once when the stream has no B-VOP.

H.263 picture headers are parsed with the extended picture type
(PLUSPTYPE), keeping its options until the next UFEP, and Sorenson
Spark headers with their disposable inter pictures, which are not
used as references. These pictures are output at once.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
